@startuml seq_hmi_boot
title Pi boot: animated splash and hand-over to the HMI
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
participant "systemd (PID 1)\nwith udev" as Systemd
participant "ksphmi --splash\nksphmi-splash.service" as Splash
participant "Probe worker\n(2 Hz)" as Probe
participant "/dev/fb0\nvc4drmfb" as FB
participant "ksphmi\nksphmi.service (user)" as HMI
participant "ksphmi.ready\n/run/user/<uid>" as Ready
activate Systemd
Systemd -> Systemd : udev tags fb0 only when its name is vc4drmfb\n(the earlier simplefb fb0 is ignored)
Systemd ->> Splash : start (Type=simple, no Before=: boot and logins carry on)
activate Splash
Splash -> Ready : exists?
activate Ready
Ready --> Splash : no
deactivate Ready
Splash ->> Probe : start detached worker
activate Probe
Splash -> FB : open, FBIOPUT_VSCREENINFO
activate FB
FB --> Splash : 2520x1680, mapped
deactivate FB
loop about 8 frames per second, until ready, SIGTERM or 10 minutes
  Splash -> Splash : boot_view(probes, CLOCK_BOOTTIME)\nrestore animated regions, redraw them
  Splash -> Ready : exists?
  activate Ready
  Ready --> Splash : no
  deactivate Ready
  Splash -> FB : write changed rows
  activate FB
  FB --> Splash : written
  deactivate FB
  opt fb0 node or driver name changed
    Splash -> FB : close and reopen
    activate FB
    FB --> Splash : reopened
    deactivate FB
  end
end
Probe -> Probe : systemctl is-active multi-user.target,\ninterface address, ksphmi process (each 0.5 s)
Systemd ->> HMI : user manager (lingering) starts ksphmi.service
activate HMI
HMI -> Ready : remove stale file
activate Ready
Ready --> HMI : removed
deactivate Ready
HMI -> HMI : first frame presented (KMSDRM or fbdev)
HMI -> Ready : write after the first present
activate Ready
Ready --> HMI : written
deactivate Ready
Splash -> Ready : exists?
activate Ready
Ready --> Splash : yes
deactivate Ready
Splash ->> Probe : stop
deactivate Probe
Splash --> Systemd : exit 0 (within one frame, about 125 ms)
deactivate Splash
HMI -> FB : fbdev only: rewrite every row 1 s later
activate FB
FB --> HMI : repainted
deactivate FB
deactivate HMI
deactivate Systemd
note over Splash, HMI : The splash checks the ready file again right before each write,\nso it never paints over the HMI's first frame.
@enduml
